                <pb facs="0071" n="61" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg61"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Pacific War/927: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-10T20:00:00-03:00">December 10, 1941—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1423. Department’s rush circular, December 8, 1 a.m. In a communication this date
                    the Foreign Office states that in accordance with the wishes of our Government
                    it has recommended that the necessary measures of an internal character be taken
                    to the end that in the war in which we are engaged with Japan the latter country
                    or its allies may be prevented from making use of the communications facilities
                    of this country to endanger in any way the security of the continent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
